---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Codex Blog" description="About Codex Blog: a journal about thoughtful software and creative work.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-24">
    <p class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-accent">A short introduction</p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-[-.05em] sm:text-6xl">About this<br /><span class="text-muted">little corner.</span></h1>
    <div class="prose-post mt-10">
      <p>Codex Blog is an independent journal about making things for the web and paying attention to how they feel.</p>
      <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
      <p>Expect practical notes on software, design, creative process, and the ideas that connect them. Some posts are field notes; others are longer explorations. All are written to be useful, thoughtful, and clear.</p>
      <h2>A work in progress</h2>
      <p>This site is a small, evolving space. New writing arrives when there’s something worth sharing. If you’d like to follow along, <a href="/rss.xml">subscribe to the RSS feed</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
